    "title": "Joe Rogan questions the 'very strange' Ray J interview after Brand Risk 14 KO - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Jamie Theodosi ,\n1 hours ago\nPhoto by Carmen Mandato/Getty Images Joe Rogan has been left confused by the recent MMA event that Dana White was involved in.\nThis past Saturday despite there being no UFC action, the META Apex was in use as it was rented by Dana White ‘s friend Adin Ross who hosted his 14th Brand Risk event.\nThe bizarre event was headlined by a clash between former professional footballer, Johnny Manziel and online influencer, Bob Menery .\nHowever, it was a clash on the prelims between Ray J and Supah Hot Fire which left UFC commentator Joe Rogan extremely confused.\nJoe Rogan confused by Ray J’s post-fight interview at Brand Risk 14 In the prelims, former actor and singer Ray J took on online personality, Supah Hot Fire in a middleweight clash.\nSupah Hot Fire went on to score a vicious KO win , which has subsequently left Ray J hospitalized with concussion like symptoms and his heart slowing down.\nDespite that, it was Ray J’s comments following the fight in his post-fight interview which left people extremely confused, one of whom was Rogan.\n“Adin Ross’ thing that he does, he does Brand Risk, he has people fight, Ray J who did the p—- with Kim Kardashian, he just got knocked the f— out in an MMA fight,” Rogan said in the recent episode of his podcast .\n“Yeah (I saw his post-fight interview), yeah, they made some sort of a deal apparently, at least he was implying that the guy wasn’t gonna punch him in the face and knock him out.\n“They must have made some sort of a deal that they weren’t gonna hurt each other and they were gonna do it for money. I wonder how much he paid him.”\nIn his post-fight interview, Ray J claimed that Supah Hot Fire went against their ‘plan’ by knocking him out, which brings the integrity of the promotion into light.\nRay J reacted to being knocked out at Brand Risk 14. Credit: Adin Live/YouTube “Yeah (that’s a way to get a visit from the FBI), it also seems like you’re admitting to a crime which is maybe because he got a concussion… It seemed very real. He must’ve said ‘I’m gonna put a bunch of money on me to win, you have me win’ and he’s now like, ‘look how much money we just lost’, they were gonna split the money… We’ll see (what happens).\n“It’s crazy that he admitted it publicly, very strange… It was very real,” he continued.\nAlthough traditional sportsbooks did not accept bets on the recent Brand Risk 14 event, fans were able to wager bets through alternative channels.",
    "summary": "Photo by Carmen Mandato/Getty Images Joe Rogan has been left confused by the recent MMA event that Dana White was involved in. This past Saturday despite there being no UFC action, the META Apex was in use as it was rented by Dana White ‘s friend Adin Ross who hosted his 14th Brand Risk event. Supah Hot Fire went on to score a vicious KO win , which has subsequently left Ray J hospitalized with concussion like symptoms and his heart slowing down.",
